Subject: [PATCH] crypto: crc32c: backport standalone CRC32C to 6.12

6.12 wires CRC32C through the Crypto API: config LIBCRC32C selects
CRYPTO and CRYPTO_CRC32C, and lib/libcrc32c.c implements crc32c() on
top of a crypto shash.  That pulls CRYPTO into the dependency graph
and closes a loop with the platform networking symbols:

  LIBCRC32C -> CRYPTO -> CRYPTO_DEV_FSL_CAAM -> FSL_MC_BUS
            -> FSL_DPAA2_ETH -> PHYLINK -> PHYLIB
            -> RTL9617C_XRAM_ETH -> NETFILTER -> NF_TABLES
            -> LIBCRC32C

which makes syncconfig abort with "recursive dependency detected!".

Upstream v6.18 already solved this: LIBCRC32C is gone, net/Kconfig
gains "config NET_CRC32C / bool / select CRC32", the net side selects
NET_CRC32C, and crc32c() is a plain library function with no Crypto API
dependency.  This patch backports that shape onto 6.12:

  * drop config LIBCRC32C and lib/libcrc32c.c;
  * implement crc32c() on top of __crc32c_le() in lib/crc32.c, which
    6.12 already provides (software fallback plus the ARM64 CRC32
    extension assembly), so the result is bit-identical to the old
    shash based helper;
  * add config NET_CRC32C exactly as upstream v6.18 has it;
  * point every remaining "select LIBCRC32C" at NET_CRC32C.

Signed-off-by: likz0421 <likz0421@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/net/Kconfig
+++ b/net/Kconfig
@@ -77,6 +77,10 @@
 	depends on DMA_SHARED_BUFFER=y
 	depends on GENERIC_ALLOCATOR
 	depends on PAGE_POOL
+
+config NET_CRC32C
+	bool
+	select CRC32
 
